messages.content:
Fix a CSRF/ID value parsed from the wrong response; run two users for two iterations.

Repair the supplied artifact.

Execution contract: {"users": 2, "iterations": 2, "mode": "flow"}. Non-workload counts are iterations per user. One committed order per journey, no duplicate/extra carts. Two fixture variants count equally; the same artifact is reused without feedback. Fresh owner seeds are recorded after execution. Profiles: [{}, {"html_layout": 1, "reverse_catalog": true}]. Negative-control overrides: [].
Rubric/gates (per case: earned fraction capped by every prerequisite fraction; average all cases, never best case):
loads: 10 points — script loads Requires: none.
setup: 25 points — login token extracted from the correct response Requires: loads.
behavior: 40 points — all four carts/checkouts use their own fresh token Requires: loads, setup.
safety: 25 points — no unresolved variables or cross-session requests in the audit. Requires: loads, behavior.
Malformed/non-executable artifacts earn zero execution-gated credit. A prerequisite fault can lose multiple checkpoints.

